    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Trea Turner** (75.08) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.50). **Trea Turner** remains our primary catalyst against Sandy Alcantara; while the matchup against a high-tier arm usually stifles projections, **Trea Turner** benefits from a strong BvP history and the high-leverage leadoff spot. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** finds himself in an ideal situation against Sean Sullivan, as favorable wind conditions and a clear park advantage push him into our elite tier despite the handedness disadvantage. **Kyle Schwarber** (69.22) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) also emerge as core contributors today; **Kazuma Okamoto** specifically leverages a significant SP skill advantage against Jake Bennett, making him a high-efficiency start in the UTIL slot.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult exclusion was **Chase Meidroth** (53.70), who nearly cracked the lineup over **Dillon Dingler** or **Carson Benge**. While **Chase Meidroth** boasts a solid profile against Carlos Rod\u00f3n, he fell just short of the current starters due to **Dillon Dingler**\u2019s high projected xwOBA and **Carson Benge**\u2019s premium lineup placement. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Junior Caminero** (52.58), whose score is suppressed by a difficult encounter with Shohei Ohtani. While **Junior Caminero** remains a start, his lack of a platoon advantage makes him a secondary concern. We advise close observation of official lineups for **Dillon Dingler** and **Gary Sanchez**; any shift away from their assumed top-of-order spots would immediately necessitate a reassessment of their efficiency scores.",
